WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.133
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.200
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.300
Well, guys, the big news here
in New York City is,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.467
we finally got our
first real snowfall of the year.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.167
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:20.767
The city got hit hard with
1.8 inches of snow.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.767
1.8 inches.
Is that really a big deal?

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:27.067
I mean, I saw more white powder
in "Cocaine Bear."

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.968
You know what I'm saying?
-Oh! Whoa!

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:32.834
-Yeah, we only got 1.8 inches,
but every meteorologist was

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.534
outside pretending they
were braving the storm like,

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:38.100
"It's a blizzard
out here, Hoda!"

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.234
People playing beach volleyball
behind them.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.334
Some political news.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.167
Today, Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:47.434
released his autobiography,
"The Courage to be Free."

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:49.367
The book is already
a number-1 bestseller,

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.200
especially in Florida,
where it's literally

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.300
the only book on the shelf.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.601
"It's the only thing here."

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.400
In the book,
DeSantis admits that

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.234
he actually got married
at Disney World.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.601
-Ooh!
-Seriously.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.434
That's like finding out
Bernie Sanders got married

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:09.834
in Jeff Bezos' backyard.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.300
It's like, "Come on."

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.200
And get this -- former president
Trump criticized Fox News

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.934
for promoting Ron DeSantis
"so hard and so much."

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:21.100
At this point,
Trump's watching Fox feels like

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.367
your friend who can't stop
looking at their ex's Instagram.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.467
It's like,
"Oh, she never liked that.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.767
That's interesting.

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:30.734
Oh, looks like she's having
real fun there.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.300
Meanwhile, a new
court filing shows that

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.033
Fox Chairman Rupert Murdoch
admitted some of the network's

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:38.801
hosts endorsed false claims
about the 2020 election.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.934
Today, Fox News promised
to focus on real issues,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.601
then introduced
their newest host, Dilbert.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.601
[ Light laughter, applause ]

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:52.200
Thank you. Got it up there?
They got it up there.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.300
These are pretty tense times
for Fox News,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.133
although everyone is remaining
calm by repeating this mantra.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:59.200
"At least we're not CNN.
At least we're not CNN.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.400
At least we're not CNN."

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.634
Some more news.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.434
Following a report from
the Energy Department

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:06.334
that said COVID might have
come from a Chinese lab leak,

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.000
The White House announced that
there is no government consensus

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.634
on how the virus started.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.901
It's never good when
the government's report

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.701
on a pandemic is
just the shrug emoji.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.701
You know, it doesn't matter
if we agree on

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.133
how the pandemic started.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.801
The important thing is, we all
agree to pretend it's over.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.167
Well, listen to this.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.901
I read that The White House
is giving federal agencies

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:32.200
30 days to remove TikTok
from all government devices.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.901
Every government employee
was like,

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.200
"I guess I have no choice"

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.801
and gave their boss
30 days' notice.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.167
This is devastating.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.067
I mean, what is TikTok without
Senator Chuck Grassley?

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:43.467
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:44.801
Some business news.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:47.300
I saw that Wendy's is going to
start selling their chili

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.267
in a can at grocery stores.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.434
[ Groaning, laughter ]

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:54.367
It's perfect if you've always
thought the chili at Wendy's

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.300
was too fresh.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.667
Under ingredients, it just says,
"Ignorance is bliss."

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:03.834
Hey, did you guys see this?

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.033
A man in California filed
a lawsuit claiming

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:09.100
that he won the $2 billion
Powerball lottery,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.234
but the ticket was
stolen from him.

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.133
Then a million Americans
were like,

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.367
"Yeah, already tried it, pal.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:15.834
I mean, come on."

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:18.167
And he was like, "Yeah, I also
lost a bag of diamonds, too."

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.434
Yeah.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.501
Experts say his odds of
winning the lawsuit are

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.267
300 million-to-1.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.434
Well, guys, today is
the last day of February,

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.667
so I thought it would be nice to
give a little recap

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.534
of the entire month.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.033
♪ February came and went ♪

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.300
♪ The shortest month,
but I feel spent ♪

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.334
♪ 28 days gone so soon ♪

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:45.334
♪ Kind of like... ♪

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:46.767
-The Chinese spy balloon.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.834
-♪ Grammys, BAFTAs, Oscar noms ♪

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.000
♪ "Top Gun" did it,
good for Tom ♪

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.868
♪ Whether or not you win
that bling ♪

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.734
-♪ Angela Bassett
did the thing ♪

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.634
-♪ Super Bowl won
by the Chiefs ♪

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.634
♪ Eagles fans were
filled with grief ♪

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.701
♪ Rihanna's halftime
we were lovin' ♪

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.567
♪ She did it with a... ♪
-Bun in the oven.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:09.033
-♪ Biden gave his big address ♪

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.934
♪ State of the Union
in Congress ♪

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.901
♪ Republicans shouted
from their chairs ♪

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.133
♪ Angrier than a... ♪

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.267
-Cocaine bear.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:18.200
-♪ Valentine's did not
go great ♪

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.300
♪ You got stood up
by your date ♪

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.167
♪ Tinder tells you that
you should think about... ♪

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.367
-Retiring for good.

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.467
-♪ Marvel's "Quantumania" ♪

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:31.501
♪ "Last of Us,"
"Outer Banks-ia" ♪

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:33.334
♪ We watched them all
except our aunts ♪

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:34.801
♪ Who were drooling over... ♪

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.234
-♪ "Magic Mike, The Last Dance."

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.601
-♪ February, you short king ♪

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.501
♪ Here comes March,
it's time for spring ♪

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:42.601
♪ We'll lose money on
our brackets ♪

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:47.000
♪ Then get trashed on
St. Patrick's ♪

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:57.133
And, finally, guys,
it is Tuesday.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.434
It is time for "WeTweet."
Here we go.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:03.334
-♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:04.667
♪♪

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:05.667
♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.868
-Alright.
Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:10.634
This is where we, as a group,
decide something that we should

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:11.734
